  "worked_solution": "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{20}=-65$, $N=20$, and ${S}_{N}=-635$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-635 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+(-65)) \\\\ -635 & =10({a}_{1}-65) \\\\ -\\frac{635}{10} & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ -63.5 & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
